# No LFS tracking — all files stored as regular git blobs

# Force LF line endings for shell scripts and autoconf files.
# Windows git autocrlf converts to CRLF which causes R CMD check warnings:
# "Found the following shell script(s) with CR or CRLF line endings"
configure    eol=lf
configure.ac eol=lf
cleanup      eol=lf
cleanup.ucrt eol=lf
*.sh         eol=lf

# Generated diff — never 3-way merge (produces diff-of-a-diff garbage on rebase).
# On conflict, pick a side and regenerate with `just templates-approve`. See CLAUDE.md.
patches/templates.patch -merge

# Cargo.lock is routed to the mx-regen merge driver
# (scripts/merge-driver-regen.sh). With the driver installed
# (`just merge-drivers-install`), a conflict that is only pin-line churn keeps
# the current side's pins and queues the lock for `just regenerate-merged`;
# any other lock conflict stops as usual. Without the driver, git falls back to
# its default text merge, as before. The `-merge` paths (above and in
# rpkg/.gitattributes) are routed to the driver by the install recipe instead,
# through .git/info/attributes. See CLAUDE.md "Rebase conflicts".
rpkg/src/rust/Cargo.lock merge=mx-regen
